WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.417 --> 00:00:02.878
♪♪

00:00:02.878 --> 00:00:07.090
Shouldn’t all that matters be...
the moment we’re living in right
now?

00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:10.010
No.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:12.971
(Phone ringing)

00:00:12.971 --> 00:00:14.514
Hi, this is Joshua Corman.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:17.392
Josh Corman sounds sort of like
Joseph Gordon.

00:00:17.518 --> 00:00:18.560
He’s not me,

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.979
but I started imagining what my
life could have been like. 

00:00:20.979 --> 00:00:21.897
So, what do you do?

00:00:23.273 --> 00:00:25.275
I teach 5th grade.

00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:26.735
Shut up, I love you.

00:00:26.735 --> 00:00:28.570
Joseph:
Having him be a teacher 

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:31.782
Joseph:
was something that I’ve always
kind of wanted to do.

00:00:31.782 --> 00:00:33.408
And the story of Mr. Corman is

00:00:33.408 --> 00:00:36.036
Joseph:
what if some things had turned
out a little different in my life.

00:00:36.495 --> 00:00:37.079
David:
Punch buggy!

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:37.955
- Okay!
- David.

00:00:37.955 --> 00:00:39.873
You have always had something
against David.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.875
I don’t have anything against
David, he’s just a bad person.

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:42.668
He’s seven.

00:00:42.668 --> 00:00:44.962
Yeah, but you can be a bad person
when you’re seven.

00:00:44.962 --> 00:00:46.463
♪♪

00:00:46.463 --> 00:00:49.633
Joseph:
Josh had certain ideas about
what he thought his life 

00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:52.761
Joseph:
was going to be like as he
arrived in adulthood

00:00:52.761 --> 00:00:54.054
Joseph:
that haven’t panned out

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.890
and he's kind of wrestling with
that.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:00.310
Well I wouldn't have agreed to go
on a date with... an actual
musician.

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:03.397
Right, well then I'm your
guy...(Nervous laugh)

00:01:04.481 --> 00:01:05.399
Joseph:
What I was trying to do

00:01:05.399 --> 00:01:06.608
Joseph:
when I was writing the show 

00:01:06.608 --> 00:01:10.195
Joseph:
was just trying to be honest and
true and real.

00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:11.530
(Screams)

00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:15.742
That’s universal. We’re all
trying to figure out who we are,
where we fit.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:16.493
Victor:
What’s bothering you?

00:01:16.493 --> 00:01:19.955
Every thought that I have I’m
like, did I lock my car?

00:01:19.955 --> 00:01:20.998
Should I go check?

00:01:20.998 --> 00:01:22.916
But, what if I trip on my way to
check?

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.835
So then should I just leave my
car unlocked?

00:01:24.835 --> 00:01:27.629
Wow, we went...I think we went
too narrow on that one.

00:01:27.629 --> 00:01:29.965
Even like the saddest moments
have a bit of comedy

00:01:29.965 --> 00:01:32.050
to it and I don’t think this
show shies away from that.

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.803
(Laughing)

00:01:34.803 --> 00:01:35.595
Woman:
That’s not funny.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:36.847
(Laughing)

00:01:36.847 --> 00:01:39.057
Obviously it is, come on.

00:01:39.057 --> 00:01:41.059
That’s why it strikes me as so
real and genuine.

00:01:42.311 --> 00:01:45.147
Josh is someone who just loves
his creativity,

00:01:45.147 --> 00:01:46.523
you know, his music.

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:48.150
♪♪

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.402
Juno:
Music is an important theme all
the way through

00:01:50.402 --> 00:01:53.780
Juno:
because it is something that
Josh really cares about 

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.074
and ultimately, I suppose walked
away from.

00:01:56.491 --> 00:01:59.244
From dark times comes great art,
as they say.

00:01:59.244 --> 00:02:01.246
Do they say that?

00:02:01.246 --> 00:02:02.497
♪♪

00:02:02.497 --> 00:02:03.915
Playback one more time.

00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:06.084
Joseph:
I created the show, you could
say.

00:02:06.084 --> 00:02:07.461
I wrote it and directed it.

00:02:07.461 --> 00:02:08.503
-Great.
-Yo.

00:02:08.503 --> 00:02:10.130
Joseph:
But definitely took a whole
bunch of

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:13.133
Joseph:
other incredibly talented
artists to make it.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.051
Joseph:
It wasn’t just me.

00:02:14.051 --> 00:02:17.387
Jason:
One of things that is so special
about working with Joe

00:02:17.387 --> 00:02:20.974
is that he has this huge amount
of respect for everyone around
him.

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:24.353
Movie making is ultimately
collaborative.

00:02:24.353 --> 00:02:24.936
Man:
Good shot.

00:02:24.936 --> 00:02:26.396
Joseph:
And the more collaborators

00:02:26.396 --> 00:02:29.399
I brought in, the better the
show got.

00:02:29.399 --> 00:02:30.359
(Laughing)

00:02:30.359 --> 00:02:31.318
I have it really good.

00:02:32.486 --> 00:02:34.946
It just... it doesn’t always
feel that way, I guess.

00:02:35.489 --> 00:02:37.407
Ruth:
Well, whose fault is that?

00:02:38.742 --> 00:02:39.493
Thanks, Mom.

00:02:39.493 --> 00:02:42.662
♪♪

